    },
    "body": "Affects `ScepClient.CertReq` in `app/src/main/java/systems/sieber/droid_scep/ScepClient.java`.\n\nI found that enrollment passed the configured RSA key size directly to `KeyPairGenerator.initialize(int)`. A measured 8192-bit value reached that call, even though the analysis tool’s RSA rule permits 3072 and 4096.\n\nI added a shared RSA key-size check before key generation and applied it to the enrollment UI, saved settings, spinner choices, and application restrictions. Unsupported or malformed values are reported and cannot start enrollment; permitted values are preserved unchanged. The provider-neutral RSA generator flow remains unchanged.\n\nI found this while running the app under RVSec, a runtime checker for how apps use the Java crypto and TLS APIs.\n\nThe project builds with this change (`:app:assembleGoogleDebug`).\n\nI'm a Computer Engineering student at the University of Brasília (UnB), working on a research project on Android app analysis. Happy to adjust this to the project's conventions.",
